            "review_title": "Review at Pho Nho 162",
            "review_text": "JSTrip_77\nSarajevo, Bosnia and Herzegovina1194 contributions\n0\nGreat Local Spot\nDec 2018 • Solo\nI've biked past this utilitarian looking restaurant on numerous occasions and finally had the chance to stop in. The food is fresh. The meat just seems to be a higher quality than some pho restaurants. This is a place that always seems to attract a decent local crowd in addition to the occasional expat so I had a feeling that it wouldn't disappoint. The prices are pretty much standard based on the types of meat that you get. I had the rare and well-done beef which cost 35,000. That, again, is standard across most of the city. I didn't realize that I could ask for veggies to be added. I learned that from the only previous posting. I'll try that next time. \n\nBut, I do agree that the broth is excellent. The noodles were perfect. And, the garlic sauce on the table was clear indicating that it wasn't recycled for a long period of time (fresher than normal). I'll certainly go back and will bring friends!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten December 29, 2018",
